Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their purpose, and typical filter / join conditions
• Students.StudentID : joins students to the grades they earned  
• Students.StudLastName : the last name we must return  
• Student_Schedules.StudentID : joins to Students  
• Student_Schedules.ClassID  : joins to Classes  
• Student_Schedules.ClassStatus : filter for 2 (Completed)  
• Student_Schedules.Grade : numeric grade used for ranking  
• Classes.ClassID : joins Student_Schedules → Classes  
• Classes.SubjectID : joins Classes → Subjects  
• Subjects.SubjectID : joins to Classes  
• Subjects.CategoryID : filter for 'ENG' to keep only English courses  

Key conditions  
• Student_Schedules.ClassStatus = 2  (completed)  
• Subjects.CategoryID = 'ENG'        (English courses only)  

Below are 10 exploratory → final‐answer queries (all limited to 20 rows for safety).

```sql
-- 1. Look up the description of the English category (expect CategoryID = 'ENG').
SELECT DISTINCT "CategoryID", "CategoryDescription"
FROM "Categories"
WHERE "CategoryDescription" LIKE '%English%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Verify there really is a CategoryID = 'ENG' in the Subjects table.
SELECT DISTINCT "CategoryID"
FROM "Subjects"
WHERE "CategoryID" = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. See a few English subjects to confirm data.
SELECT "SubjectID", "SubjectCode", "SubjectName"
FROM "Subjects"
WHERE "CategoryID" = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Show some completed English classes with the raw grades recorded.
SELECT ss."StudentID", ss."ClassID", ss."Grade"
FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN "Classes"         AS c ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN "Subjects"        AS s ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
WHERE ss."ClassStatus" = 2          -- completed
  AND s."CategoryID"   = 'ENG'      -- English
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Add students’ last names to the same information.
SELECT st."StudLastName", ss."Grade"
FROM   "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN   "Classes"           AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN   "Subjects"          AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
JOIN   "Students"          AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
WHERE  ss."ClassStatus" = 2
  AND  s."CategoryID"   = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. How many completed‑English grade records exist?  (Needed for quintile math.)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "total_completed_english_grades"
FROM   "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN   "Classes"           AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN   "Subjects"          AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
WHERE  ss."ClassStatus" = 2
  AND  s."CategoryID"   = 'ENG';
```

```sql
-- 7. Give each record a rank (1 = best grade) and show the running count.
SELECT st."StudLastName",
       ss."Grade",
       RANK()  OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC)     AS "grade_rank",
       COUNT(*) OVER ()                            AS "total"
FROM   "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN   "Classes"           AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN   "Subjects"          AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
JOIN   "Students"          AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
WHERE  ss."ClassStatus" = 2
  AND  s."CategoryID"   = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Translate that rank into a percentile (rank / total).
SELECT st."StudLastName",
       ss."Grade",
       RANK()  OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC)     AS "grade_rank",
       ROUND(1.0 * RANK() OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC) /
                 COUNT(*) OVER (), 4)              AS "pct_rank"
FROM   "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN   "Classes"           AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN   "Subjects"          AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
JOIN   "Students"          AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
WHERE  ss."ClassStatus" = 2
  AND  s."CategoryID"   = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Use NTILE(5) to break the ordered list into five equal buckets (quintiles).
SELECT st."StudLastName",
       ss."Grade",
       NTILE(5) OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC)    AS "quintile_num"
FROM   "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN   "Classes"           AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN   "Subjects"          AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
JOIN   "Students"          AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
WHERE  ss."ClassStatus" = 2
  AND  s."CategoryID"   = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: last names + labeled quintiles, sorted First → Fifth.
SELECT st."StudLastName"                               AS "LastName",
       CASE NTILE(5) OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC)
            WHEN 1 THEN 'First'   -- top  0‑20 %
            WHEN 2 THEN 'Second'  -- top 21‑40 %
            WHEN 3 THEN 'Third'   -- top 41‑60 %
            WHEN 4 THEN 'Fourth'  -- top 61‑80 %
            ELSE 'Fifth'          -- bottom 20 %
       END                                            AS "Quintile"
FROM   "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN   "Classes"           AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN   "Subjects"          AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
JOIN   "Students"          AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
WHERE  ss."ClassStatus" = 2
  AND  s."CategoryID"   = 'ENG'
ORDER BY
       CASE NTILE(5) OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC)
            WHEN 1 THEN 1
            WHEN 2 THEN 2
            WHEN 3 THEN 3
            WHEN 4 THEN 4
            ELSE 5
       END
LIMIT 20;
```

